  "notes": "FORMS:\n{仮|かり} (temporary) + {眠|みん} (sleep) → temporary sleep\n{仮眠|かみん}する (to take a nap)\n{仮眠|かみん}を{取|と}る (to take a nap)\n\nRELATED FACILITIES:\n- {仮眠室|かみんしつ} (nap room)\n- {仮眠|かみん}スペース (nap space)\n\nDIFFERENCE FROM OTHER SLEEP WORDS:\n- {昼寝|ひるね} (afternoon nap) - casual, usually at home\n- {仮眠|かみん} (nap) - more formal, can be at work\n- うたた{寝|ね} (dozing off) - unintentional, light sleep\n- {居眠|いねむ}り (nodding off) - falling asleep while sitting\n\nWORKPLACE CONTEXT:\nMany Japanese companies now recognize the benefits of napping and provide {仮眠室|かみんしつ} (nap rooms) for employees. Power naps of 15-20 minutes are recommended for productivity.",
